    <title>Physical Exam</title>
    <text><paragraph>Vital signs recorded on 1977-03-17; see the Vital Signs section. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>General</td><td>Tired but alert and oriented; speaking easily; not toxic</td></tr><tr><td>Cardiovascular</td><td>Heart rate 98 and regular; blood pressure 118/70 mm Hg; capillary refill normal</td></tr><tr><td>Respiratory</td><td>Respiratory rate 18; clear to auscultation</td></tr><tr><td>Abdomen</td><td>Soft; mild tenderness in the right flank and right costovertebral angle; no peritoneal signs; healed midline incision</td></tr><tr><td>Stoma</td><td>Pink, moist, budded about 1.5 cm; no retraction, necrosis, or bleeding; peristomal skin intact; no parastomal bulge on coughing; cloudy urine in the bag</td></tr><tr><td>Mucous membranes</td><td>Slightly dry</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

