    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acute right pyelonephritis with an ileal conduit, with mild acute kidney injury (N10)</content>. Fever, flank tenderness, leukocytosis (white cell count 12.6), and pyuria (55 white cells per high-power field) point to an upper-tract infection rather than the harmless bacteriuria that is expected in conduit urine. He is not septic: alert, blood pressure 118/70 mm Hg, respiratory rate 18. Creatinine 1.41 mg/dL is up from 1.12, from infection and low intake. He is able to drink and has had no fluoroquinolone in the past year, so oral treatment at home is reasonable. [S]<list><item>Urine for culture taken today by sterile catheter through the stoma, not from the bag.</item><item>Ciprofloxacin 500 mg twice daily for 7 days, adjusted to the culture result.</item><item>At least 2.5 liters of fluid a day while febrile; acetaminophen for fever; avoid ibuprofen and other NSAIDs while creatinine is raised.</item><item>Repeat creatinine and chemistry in one week.</item><item>Renal ultrasound if the fever has not settled within 48 to 72 hours, to look for obstruction at the ureteric anastomoses.</item><item>Go to the emergency department for vomiting, rigors, confusion, or lightheadedness.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Ileal conduit urostomy (Z93.6)</content>. Stoma healthy and appliance sealing well. [S]<list><item>Night drainage bag to keep the conduit draining freely while he recovers.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Holzbeierlein J, et al. Treatment of Non-Metastatic Muscle-Invasive Bladder Cancer: AUA/ASCO/SUO Guideline (2017; Amended 2020, 2024). J Urol 2024;212(1):3-10 (2024); Trautner BW, et al. IDSA 2025 Guideline Update on Complicated Urinary Tract Infections (2025)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Nurse telephone check in 48 hours with the culture result. Creatinine recheck in one week. Return or call the same day for worsening symptoms. Next scheduled visit 1977-04-07: six-month post-cystectomy follow-up: kidney function, acid-base, upper-tract ultrasound, and review after a kidney infection. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
